title: WordPress Core Upgrade-Window RCE (CVE-2026-119977) — Direct Request to Unpacked Installer PHP
id: 5a2e7f19-40cb-4c86-b1d3-9e8f2a6c7d51
status: experimental
description: >
  Detects an HTTP request for a PHP file inside the WordPress core upgrade working directory.
  CVE-2026-119977 (CVSS 8.1, WordPress 4.7 through 7.1.3, fixed in 7.1.4) is exploitable during
  the brief window of a full-package core upgrade: the downloaded package is unpacked into a
  predictable, web-accessible path, letting an unauthenticated attacker reach the installer
  scripts and execute code. WordPress never serves files from this directory, so any request
  for a PHP file beneath it is attacker traffic or an administrator fetching security/upgrade
  directories directly. Patchstack observed roughly 63,000 exploitation attempts shortly
  after disclosure.
references:
  - https://suriq.io/blog/wordpress-core-cve-2026-119977-upgrade-window-rce
  - https://patchstack.com/articles/wordpress-7-1-4-security-release/
  - https://wordpress.org/news/2026/10/wordpress-7-1-4/
  - https://thehackernews.com/2026/10/wordpress-rce-flaw-draws-nearly-63000.html
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/10/31
tags:
  - attack.t1190
  - attack.t1059
  - attack.t1595
logsource:
  category: webserver
detection:
  selection_upgrade_dir:
    cs-uri|contains: '/wp-content/upgrade/'
  selection_php_file:
    cs-uri|endswith: '.php'
  selection_browse:
    cs-method:
      - GET
      - POST
  condition: all of selection_*
falsepositives:
  - Administrator or deployment tooling fetching the core upgrade directory directly during maintenance
  - Migration, backup or integrity-check plugins that enumerate files under wp-content
level: high
